HuseyinUtkuASLAN/Hopfield-Network | stars=1 | https://github.com/HuseyinUtkuASLAN/Hopfield-Network | A Hopfield network is a form of recurrent artificial neural network popularized by John Hopfield in 1982, but described earlier by Little in 1974. Hopfield nets serve as content-addressable memory systems with binary threshold nodes.
1hubert/hopfield-network | stars=0 | https://github.com/1hubert/hopfield-network | Python implementation of an Asynchronous Hopfield Network for associative memory, based on the 1982 paper by J. J. Hopfield
